<title>FRANCE: TABLE-French consumer spending down 2.9 pct in Jun.</title>
<headline>TABLE-French consumer spending down 2.9 pct in Jun.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE gave the following seasonally adjusted figures for household spending on manufactured goods in billions of 1980 francs:</p>
<p>				   June    May    April    March</p>
<p> Total			   56.36  58.04   58.36    57.88</p>
<p> Total change (pct m/m)    -2.9    -0.5     0.8	0.3</p>
<p> Retail sector		 38.32  39.42   39.31    38.49</p>
<p> Durables			15.91  16.89   17.27    16.75</p>
<p> Textiles, leather	   10.88  11.45   11.51    11.44</p>
<p> Other			   29.56  29.71   29.58    29.70</p>
<p>It gave the following percentage changes (month-on-month</p>
<p>unless stated)</p>
<p>				June    May    April   June yr/yr</p>
<p> Total			-2.9   -0.5     0.8     -4.4</p>
<p> Retail sector	    -2.8    0.3     2.1     -2.0</p>
<p> Durables		   -5.8   -2.2     3.1    -11.4</p>
<p>   of which cars	 -10.7   -7.9    -1.5    -28.2</p>
<p>   household equip	-3.2    1.2     6.1	0.2</p>
<p> Textiles, leather	-5.0   -0.5     0.6     -6.2</p>
<p> Other			-0.5    0.4    -0.4	0.5</p>
<p>NOTE - INSEE said in its statement on the figures that spending had been negatively affected by the structure of business days in June, which had four Saturdays compared with five Sundays.</p>
<p>The five percent decline in textile and leather purchases was affected by a shift in the start of seasonal sales.</p>
<p>Consumer spending fell 0.5 percent in the second quarter after rising 0.6 percent in the first quarter.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
